WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
Thanks for tuning in to Planetarian Daily, episode 87 coming to you on June 12th, 2026.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.780
Some interesting findings to cover today. Electric fish research reveals a single brain hub

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:18.120
that times sensory predictions during self-generated actions. Biologists at Washington University in

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:24.640
St. Louis examined corollary discharge in electric fish. A copy of motor commands sent to sensory

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.180
areas. The study published in current biology shows this signal routes through one central hub rather than

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:37.100
distributed pathways. Fish use the mechanism to distinguish self-produced electric signals from

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:43.140
external ones in milliseconds. The work clarifies how nervous systems solve the agency problem

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.220
across vertebrates. Follow-up experiments will test whether the hub generalizes to mammalian

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:55.880
auditory and visual systems. The Planetarian Spotlight this week focuses on how this single timing hub

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:01.320
might translate to human imaging protocols that could clarify sensory gating issues.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.980
Now shifting from timing mechanisms in the brain to another internal sensing system that also operates

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:15.160
largely below awareness. Interoception tracks heartbeat, respiration, and gut signals via vagal and

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:21.580
spinal routes to insular and somal testering cortices. The hidden sense monitors these signals without

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:27.860
conscious attention according to the mapping described in recent reviews. Disruptions in interoceptive

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:34.180
accuracy appear in anxiety, eating disorders, and certain chronic pain states. Training protocol

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.780
is that improved heartbeat detection have shown modest symptom reduction in small trials.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.960
Larger studies are testing whether targeted interoceptive feedback improves emotion regulation.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:51.280
The open access platform constructs subject specific brain models from multimodal imaging and

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:57.620
electrophysiological data. Simulations allow testing of stimulation protocols or disease progression

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:03.980
without invasive procedures. Validation against held out recordings shows accurate reproduction of

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:09.780
resting state networks. The resources intended for both research and eventual clinical planning

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:15.800
applications. On a different note, from real-time internal sensing to longer-term physiological

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:24.280
patterns tracked over decades, a 30-year follow-up of more than 147,000 adults found that 90 to 120

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:29.960
minutes of resistance exercise correlated with reduced death from cardiovascular and neurological

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:36.060
causes. The observational design tracked self-reported activity and verified outcomes through

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:42.740
national registries. Adding aerobic activity further lowered risk beyond strength training along.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:50.420
Those response curves plateaued above 120 minutes per week. Replication and randomized trials

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:57.240
is now being planned. A randomized placebo-controlled trial tested the dopamine agonist in patient's

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:02.220
meeting criteria for major depressive disorder, dysthemia, or bipolar depression.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:08.320
Promethexol produced statistically significant drops on the Snafe Hamilton pleasure scale

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:14.480
relative to placebo. Target engagement was confirmed through changes in reward-related

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:20.600
neural responses. The study enrolled participants across multiple sites with standardized diagnostic

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:26.720
assessments. Larger phase three trials will examine durability and long-term safety.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:33.800
Life biosciences injected an experimental reprogramming therapy into the eye of a patient with

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:40.080
glaucoma. The treatment aims to regenerate retinal ganglion cells by resetting epigenetic

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:47.120
age in nerve tissue. Partial reprogramming avoids full-induced pluripotent stem cell conversion

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:54.360
to limit tumor risk. Early safety monitoring will track inter-ocular pressure and visual field changes.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:58.520
Additional cohorts are planned for other age-related eye conditions.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:04.540
Prior outbreak suffered when burial and mourning practices were ignored by response teams.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.620
The commentary details how traditional rights can be adapted to reduce transmission while respecting

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:17.100
community needs. Successful models from earlier epidemics incorporated local leaders in safe body

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:23.360
handling protocols. Authors argue that exclusion of religious networks prolonged chains of infection.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.860
Current DRC and Uganda responses are incorporating these lessons in real-time.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:35.480
From activity patterns that influence lifespan to cellular processes that accumulate damage over time.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:42.520
A review in cell synthesizes evidence that stochastic epigenetic changes plus chronic stress

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:49.340
push cells into irreversible senescence. Senescence cells then secrete factors that propagate

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:55.520
dysfunction to neighboring tissues. The authors discuss interventions that clear or reprogram these

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:01.320
cells as upstream approaches to multiple age-related diseases. They highlight remaining gaps in

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:08.080
human biomarker validation and tissue-specific timing. From cellular-level aging markers to proteins

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:14.740
shed by senescent cells that can be measured in circulation. Proteomic profiling identified proteins

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:19.260
shed by senescent cells that circulate and correlate with future health outcomes.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:25.200
The accompanying cell atlas maps which tissues contribute most to the circulating pool.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:31.600
Several candidates improved prediction of mortality and multi-morbidity beyond standard clinical

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:39.060
scores. Independent cohorts are being assembled to confirm generalizability. Researchers at Germany's

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:44.380
Federal Institute for Materials Research and Testing propose redesigning battery and turbine

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:50.360
components from the outset. The perspective argues that early choices in chemistry and architecture

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:57.020
improve recyclability and cut reliance on scarce elements. Modeling shows performance retention

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:03.300
can be maintained while lowering raw material intensity. Pilot projects will test these principles

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:09.740
in hydrogen and wind technologies. The perspective outlines methods to combine fine-grained city

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:15.920
measurements with Earth system models. Authors emphasize translating interdisciplinary data sets into

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:22.260
equitable policy without losing local context. The approach addresses gaps between climate projections

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:29.120
and actionable urban interventions. Case examples focus on emissions, heat islands, and infrastructure

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:35.080
resilience. Implementation will require new data sharing standards across municipal agencies.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:42.760
High-resolution simulations from ICTA-UAB forecast altered sea land breeze patterns by 2050

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:49.200
and 2100. Weaker and nighttime land breezes are expected to trap pollutants over the metropolitan

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:55.320
area. The study links these circulation shifts to increased surface ozone concentrations.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:01.480
Health risk estimates include additional respiratory and cardiovascular burden for millions of

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:07.180
residents. Adaptation strategies under discussion include expanded urban greening and traffic

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:13.820
controls. The international study demonstrates that fish are not passive responders but modify flow

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:19.520
and sediment dynamics through their behavior. Human-made channels select for different swimming

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:25.560
and foraging traits that in turn alter erosion patterns. Feedback loops between evolved fish

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:31.420
populations and physical river structure are now documented. Management plans that ignore these

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:38.380
biological feedbacks risk repeated restoration failures. From internal biological signals to external

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:45.000
environmental exposures now detectable through plant tissue, sampling near conflict zones in southern

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:51.180
Israel showed substantially higher PFAS concentrations in potato leaves than in surrounding soils.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:58.240
The pattern points to atmospheric deposition rather than root uptake as the dominant recent exposure

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:03.800
root. Researchers suggest plants can serve as sensitive sentinels for ongoing contamination.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.940
Expanded surveys will test the approach across additional crop species and regions.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:14.900
From environmental detection methods to engineered systems that actively process pollutants.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:21.060
Researchers engineered a solar-driven material that uses one photon to drive two linked reactions.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:28.180
The catalyst simultaneously reduces carbon dioxide and oxidizes organic waste, yielding useful

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:34.040
chemicals from both streams. The approach avoids separate energy inputs for each half reaction.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:40.120
Performance data shows stable operation under visible light without precious metal co-catalysts.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:44.480
Next steps include scaling the material for continuous flow reactors.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.620
You've probably heard that the brain simply reacts to whatever arrives through the senses,

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.960
but here's what's actually happening. Right now, as you shift posture or turn a page,

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.900
an internal copy of the motor command reaches sensory areas milliseconds ahead of the actual feedback.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:06.540
The electric fish work shows this predictive signal funnels through one compact timing hub

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:11.760
rather than many parallel routes. When the mechanism is experimentally disrupted,

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:17.320
animals treat their own actions as external events and generate unnecessary responses.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:23.740
The practical takeaway is that many sensory and motor symptoms may trace to timing mismatches

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:30.160
in this prediction system rather than outright sensory loss. Before we go, keep an eye on expanded

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.640
surveys testing potato leaves and other crops as sentinels for airborne contaminants in additional

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:42.020
regions. That's planetary and daily for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating or review on Apple

